Adapted files:

- crates/confidant-core/src/error.rs
  DomainError taxonomy, typed downcast via DomainError::of, stable codes,
  internal_error for unclassified failures, and usage-error exit 2. Confidant
  adds file/line/fix fields and E_* codes (ADR-7, ADR-13).

- crates/confidant-core/src/check.rs
  Severity (two levels), Finding with a stable code(), CheckSummary::fails,
  CheckReport deterministic order, and parse_fail_on / --fail-on. The scanner
  itself is original.

- crates/confidant-core/src/paths.rs
  Refuse symbolic links, classify directory entries without following them,
  and write atomically via a uniquely named temporary file plus rename, then
  fsync the parent directory. Unix (including macOS) uses the openat /
  O_NOFOLLOW walk from cr. The portable symlink_metadata fallback is compiled
  only for non-Unix targets.

- crates/confidant-crypt/src/aead.rs
  XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD with length-prefixed associated data. Confidant
  re-keys to per-client data keys and binds vault_id, record ULID, client
  id, path, purpose, epoch, and the outer header in the AAD (ADR-13).

Re-implemented patterns (no cr source copied; credited per ADR-13):

- Collect findings instead of aborting on the first damaged file.
- Crash-safe write: publish via rename so a crash cannot leave a half-written
  record as the canonical file.
- Classify errors by typed downcast, never by message text.

The following cr pieces are deliberately not used: the linear audit chain,
database.rs, schema-driven field encryption, sync.rs, and anything server or
UI related. Encryption code is out of scope for milestone 1 (section 9b).

